{"name":"Common Feldspar","hex":"#858f94","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"common","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Mutual; shared by more than one.","(of a quality) Existing among virtually all people; universal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Mutual good, shared by more than one.","A tract of land in common ownership; common land."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/common"},{"term":"feldspar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a large group of rock-forming aluminosilicate minerals containing potassium, sodium, or calcium that, together, make up about 60% of the Earth's outer crust."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feldspar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Feldspar","blocks":[{"text":"Feldspar is a group of rock-forming aluminium tectosilicate minerals, also containing other cations such as sodium, calcium, potassium, or barium. The most common members of the feldspar group are the plagioclase (sodium-calcium) feldspars and the alkali (potassium-sodium) feldspars. Feldspars make up about 60% of the Earth's crust and 41% of the Earth's continental crust by weight."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Feldspar_diversity.png/330px-Feldspar_diversity.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feldspar","wikidata":"Q170258"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Anorthite_crankshaft.png/120px-Anorthite_crankshaft.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Anorthite_crankshaft.png/250px-Anorthite_crankshaft.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Anorthite_crankshaft.png/120px-Anorthite_crankshaft.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont